.TH CLOG_SET_FIELD 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
clog_set_field \- attach or update a persistent structured field
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <clogger.h>

void clog_set_field(clog logger, const char *key, const char *value);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Associates key with value as a persistent field. The field appears in
every subsequent log line emitted by this logger, inserted between the
func= and msg= tokens:

  ts=... level=INFO proc=prog(pid):tname(tid) src=... func=... key=value msg=...

Both key and value are copied internally; the caller may free or
modify them after this call without affecting the logger.

If key already exists its value is replaced. Otherwise a new field is
added to the field set.

A key must consist entirely of printable US-ASCII characters
(0x21-0x7e) excluding '=', ']', '"', and '\e\e'; a key that is empty,
contains any of those excluded characters, contains whitespace or an
ASCII control character, or contains any non-ASCII byte is silently
ignored. So is a key that names one of the fixed tokens every log
line already carries: ts, level, proc, src, func, msg, bt, bt_error.
Allowing one of those through would produce a duplicate key= token in
logfmt, a duplicate JSON key, or a duplicate RFC 5424 SD-PARAM-NAME
within the same SD-ELEMENT.

Values that contain spaces, '=', '"', '\e\e', or ASCII control
characters are automatically double-quoted and backslash-escaped in
the output:
  - '"' -> \e"
  - '\e\e' -> \e\e
  - control chars -> \exNN

The exact escape syntax differs by output format (see
clog_set_format(3)): JSON uses \euNNNN Unicode escapes, and RFC 5424
syslog escapes '"', '\e\e', and ']' in addition to control characters.
When the output format is CLOG_FMT_JSON, a value that is not
well-formed UTF-8 has each invalid byte replaced with the Unicode
replacement character (U+FFFD) rather than being embedded raw, since
JSON text must be valid Unicode.
An RFC 5424 SD-PARAM-NAME longer than 32 characters is shortened to
its first 23 characters followed by '~' and an 8-hex-digit hash of the
full key, rather than a bare 32-character prefix, so two distinct long
keys sharing a common prefix still get distinct SD-PARAM-NAMEs.
In every format, control characters (including a literal newline or
carriage return) are always neutralized, so a field value can never
split a single record across multiple lines.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
logger  Logger handle.
key     Field name. Copied internally. Silently ignored if empty,
        invalid, or one of the reserved names listed above.
value   Field value. Copied internally. May be arbitrary text.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Thread-safe: protected by the per-logger mutex.
Every emitted line visits each attached field once; keep the field
count small if logging is a hot path.
Asserts if logger is CLOG_INVALID, stale, or already closed.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clog_remove_field (3),
.BR clog_clear_fields (3)
